course: dictionary
lesson: 14894
title: Reconstructed: built again or pieced together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Reconstructed comes from reconstruct, which means to build something again or to put it back together. It has two main meanings: built again after being damaged, or worked out from clues. «The old town hall was reconstructed after the flood.» Here the hall was built again.
explain: The second meaning is about clues. «The police reconstructed the robbery from camera footage and witness stories.» Nobody saw every moment, so the police pieced the story together, the way you might put a jigsaw together.
explain: As an adjective, reconstructed describes a copy built to show how something used to look. «We walked round a reconstructed Iron Age house at the museum.» A reconstructed object is not the original, but it helps us picture the past.
fact: Reconstructed means built again after being damaged or destroyed.
fact: Reconstructed can also mean worked out or pieced together from clues.
fact: A reconstructed object is a copy, not the original.
fact: «Reconstructed» is the past tense of «reconstruct»: «Yesterday the team reconstructed the old bridge.»
fact: Scientists reconstructed what dinosaurs looked like from their fossils.
exercise: «After the earthquake, the school was reconstructed.» What does reconstructed mean here? | Moved to the seaside | Painted bright blue | Knocked down for ever | *Built again after being damaged
exercise: «Detectives reconstructed the crime from witness stories and CCTV.» What did they do? | *Pieced together what happened from clues | Painted the crime scene | Forgot the crime completely | Built a new police station
exercise: «We saw a reconstructed Iron Age house at the museum.» What is a reconstructed house? | *A copy built to show how a house used to look | A house that was never built | A house made of ice | The original house from the Iron Age
test: «The Viking ship at the museum was reconstructed from old wood.» Is the ship the original? | Not enough information to know | *No, it is a copy built to show how the ship looked | Yes, it is the very same ship from long ago | It is a painting of a ship
test: «Scientists reconstructed a dinosaur's face from fossils.» What does reconstructed mean here? | Bought at a shop | *Worked out from clues | Found a dinosaur alive today | Destroyed the fossils
exam: «The shop was reconstructed after the fire.» Which word is closest in meaning to reconstructed? | Sold | Painted | *Rebuilt | Burned
